Talent Programme Internship&nbsp;

Employment type: Fixed-term contract (6 Months) | Hours: 20 hours/week | Base Salary : £35,000 pro rata&nbsp;

Start Date: 14th September 2026&nbsp;

About the team

Our Field Sales Talent Acquisition team is on the front line of growing SumUp's self-employed sales force across the EU,, spanning both established and emerging markets. We're a fast-moving team with big targets, and right now we need someone who can take ownership of the operational engine that keeps our hiring running at pace.&nbsp;

As the team scales across core and new EU markets to accelerate growth, this is a real opportunity to own the operational heartbeat of a high-impact hiring function and make a measurable difference to how quickly we bring great people into SumUp.

What you'll do

• Manage and activate both internal and external referral programmes, finding creative ways to reach our self-employed talent pool and track payout reporting

• Handle the full Express Hiring process for team manager referrals, working closely with team managers to ensure screening is completed correctly

• Complete first-stage screening of all Meta lead-form applicants (averaging around 15 leads per country per day) before passing them to recruiters for interviews

• Research and test new outbound sourcing channels,&nbsp; from social media communities to university networks, to grow our candidate pipeline

• Conduct regular job board audits to keep our adverts competitive, well-positioned, and attracting the right applicants across EU markets

You'll be great for this role if…

• Strong proficiency in Excel or Google Sheets, with the ability to track referral volumes, lead data, and job board performance without heavy guidance.

• Experience managing high-volume, repeatable administrative workflows with accuracy and consistency.

• Ability to spot trends in data, such as referral conversion rates or lead response times, and flag insights to the wider team.

• Comfort working across multiple tools and platforms simultaneously, staying organised when priorities shift.

• A proactive, structured approach to work, with a genuine sense of ownership over the tasks you take on.

&nbsp;

🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our central London Bridge location,This involves an office-first setup&nbsp;

🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone's perspectives are respected and embraced&nbsp;

🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave (pro rota), plus bank holidays and special leaves&nbsp;

📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;D budget for attending conferences and/or advancing your career through further education&nbsp;

